  **External review — v14 manuscript**

  Overall: [2-3 sentences]. The revision is unusually transparent... The central matched comparison is internally consistent (checked against summary.csv/contrasts.csv)... Main residual defects below.

  **Major**

  1. **Informative censoring excluded from OOD metrics.** IT505 E. coli MBC (>500 mg/L) is dropped from all exact-value OOD metrics; the headline pooled MAE/RMSE (1.649/2.054) is thus computed on 67/68 values, and the dropped point is the largest failure (all human predictions 21–37 mg/L vs >500). MIC censoring is informative — ">500" typically denotes inactivity — so excluding censored points biases OOD error estimates downward exactly where absolute prediction matters. Fix: report a bound-aware metric (hinge error max(0, log2(500)−log2 ŷ)) alongside exact-value metrics, and state explicitly whether any historical QAC workbook values were converted from bounds.

  2. **Unresolved annotation provenance (H1–H7) gates the central interpretation.** If annotators saw the MIC/MBC values later used as quantitative supervision (H4), "human judgement" is not an independent supervisory channel and the human-vs-MIC comparison partly contrasts measurement-derived signals; the direction of bias is not signable ex ante. Until H1–H7 are completed, the claim "human Good/Bad calls can serve as molecular supervision" should be labelled provisional. Fix: complete H1–H7 before submission; at minimum state in the main text (not only 4.1/4.4) that blinding status is unknown.

  3. **Post-hoc narrative selection is disclosed but under-specified.** The abstract/introduction say Q-HERO was demoted "after inspection of earlier analyses," without stating what was seen. Fix: one sentence in the main text giving the direction/magnitude of the demoted results, so readers can judge selective emphasis without excavating SI. Likewise mark the scaffold-held-out real-vs-shuffled contrast ([−0.2591, −0.0001]) as hypothesis-generating in the Conclusions, not only in Results — its upper limit is a hair below zero and it is one of many unadjusted contrasts.

  4. **Uncertainty is asymmetric for the raw reference.** Raw MolFormer has a single decoder run; bootstrap intervals for human-vs-raw contrasts resample only the five trained-arm seeds (raw prediction held fixed), and bootstrapping five seed indices is coarse. The "improvement over raw features" claim therefore carries one-sided uncertainty. Fix: run the raw decoder over matched seeds/folds, or state explicitly that raw-arm decoder variability is not represented.

  5. **Training unit differs across arms and is never stated.** Human arm: one call per training molecule (377; 52 positive). MIC arms: records repeat molecules (4,938 records over 681 molecules). If continuous/binary arms train on records, molecules with more assays receive more gradient weight, and "matched source chemistry" no longer implies matched supervision size/weighting. Fix: state per-arm training-example counts and aggregation in 4.2 (per-record vs per-molecule mean log MIC).

  6. **Internal inconsistency in cation-fold construction.** 105 salts/103 cations cannot yield "five folds of 21 salts each" under cation grouping (103 is not divisible by 5; duplicated cations inflate some folds), yet "counterion forms of the same cation remain together" requires cation grouping. 21-salt folds are exact only under salt grouping, which contradicts the cation-together claim. Fix: state the actual grouping key and per-fold salt counts.

  **Minor**

  7. Text-vs-one-hot confounds task-description content with feature dimensionality (4 vs 1,536, constant within task). A control with 1,536-d random constant-per-task vectors would isolate content from dimension; alternatively relabel the condition "high-dimensional task indicators" to deter semantic readings. (The text's own caution is appreciated.)
  8. Primary inference rests on pooled RMSE across endpoints with heterogeneous variance (Sa MBC ≈1.9 vs Ec MIC ≈1.6 log2 units); pooled loss weights endpoints by their error scale. Consider per-endpoint standardized contrasts with multiplicity control as a sensitivity.

